"""A short-fragment vowel-seam detector, with a second response to numeric commas.

Adjacent vowel letters split across tokens are not equivalent: e after a/i/o/u is
strongly positive, while u-a is negative. Longer fragments and a further vowel
usually weaken the seam response. Commas immediately following decimal digits
are positive, especially after a multi-digit number rather than an identifier
or a decimal/list separator. State resets between packed documents.
