English his/he/him give the largest negative responses, then her/she, then
plural and inanimate possessives. Male person nouns and selected non-English
pronouns respond more weakly. This is a token-level rule: capitalization,
leading spaces, and whether a fragment continues a word affect its strength.

A small grammatical adjustment strengthens references after prepositions or
subordinators. The first token is weaker; thereafter strength declines with document
position and with frequent or recently repeated English third-person forms. State resets at each
new document. Unrecognized tokens predict zero.
